-- More variants: every way `T` asks a method of `A`'s `<error>` value —
-- `==` and `<` either way round, inside a list, a `Maybe`, a record and a
-- tuple, in a function and a `let` helper, `List.sort`'s requirement, and
-- a hand-written dot-call. Each wanted meets `err` and is `poisoned`: `A`'s
-- one error is the whole output, and `T` is silent with no INTERNAL ERROR
-- (checker-v2.md §12.2).
pub f = 1 + "x"
